ly! To find the product of 131755873 and 603928666, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values**:\n   ```\n   131755873\n   \u00d7 603928666\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply each digit of the second number by the first number, starting from the rightmost digit**:\n   - Start with the units place of the second number (6):\n     - 3 \u00d7 6 = 18 (write down 8 and carry over 1).\n     - 8 \u00d7 6 = 48 + 1 (carry) = 49 (write down 9 and carry over 4).\n     - 6 \u00d7 6 = 36 + 4 (carry) = 40 (write down 0 and carry over 4).\n     - 2 \u00d7 6 = 12 + 4 (carry) = 16 (write down 6 and carry over 1).\n     - 8 \u00d7 6 = 48 + 1 (carry) = 49 (write down 9 and carry over 4).\n     - 9 \u00d7 6 = 54 + 4 (carry) = 58 (write down 8 and carry over 5).\n     - 0 \u00d7 6 = 0 + 5 (carry) = 5 (write down 5).\n   - Move to the tens place of the second number (8):\n     - 3 \u00d7 8 = 24 (write down 4 and carry over 2).\n     - 8 \u00d7 8 = 64 + 2 (carry) = 66 (write down 6 and carry over 6).\n     - 6 \u00d7 8 = 48 + 6 (carry) = 54 (write down 4 and carry over 5).\n     - 2 \u00d7 8 = 16 + 5 (carry) = 21 (write down 1 and carry over 2).\n     - 8 \u00d7 8 = 64 + 2 (carry) = 66 (write down 6 and carry over 6).\n     - 9 \u00d7 8 = 72 + 6 (carry) = 78 (write down 8 and carry over 7).\n     - 0 \u00d7 8 = 0 + 7 (carry) = 7 (write down 7).\n   - Move to the hundreds place of the second number (2):\n     - 3 \u00d7 2 = 6 (write down 6).\n     - 8 \u00d7 2 = 16 (write down 6 and carry over 1).\n     - 6 \u00d7 2 = 12 + 1 (carry) = 13 (write down 3 and carry over 1).\n     - 9 \u00d7 2 = 18 + 1 (carry) = 19 (write down 9 and carry over 1).\n     - 0 \u00d7 2 = 0 + 1 (carry) = 1 (write down 1).\n   - Move to the thousands place of the second number (9):\n     - 3 \u00d7 9 = 27 (write down 7 and carry over 2).\n     - 8 \u00d7 9 = 72 + 2 (carry) = 74 (write down 4 and carry over 7).\n     - 6 \u00d7 9 = 54 + 7 (carry) = 61 (write down 1 and carry over 6).\n     - 0 \